    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.11_base_commutative_diagram.chapters.04_history_and_path_admission.sections.02_path_admission_predicate_unpacking.concrete_anchor_24_CocLegCompatibility#coclegcompatibility" .
silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_04_history_and_path_admission_sections_02_path_admission_predicate_unpacking_concrete_anchor_24_CocLegCompatibility#coclegcompatibility silm:hasLongDescription "The CocLegCompatibility is the universal cocone-leg compatibility law: all incoming legs agree on the apex. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'CocLegCompatibility', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
